<?xml version="1.0"?>
<root>
  <!--
    On boards with EC EFS2 GSC needs to know when the EC resets, so it
    can reset the EC EFS boot_mode. GSC can't tell when the EC resets if
    if it is reset with the servo EC_RST_L signal. This interferes with
    entering recovery since GSC doesn't know the EC is in RO.

    Let each servo type decide which reset to use for ec efs2
    cold_reset. servos should give a cold_reset_efs2 alias to the signal
    they should use with EC-EFS2.
      - ccd: default_cold_reset - ec_efs2 doesn't thouch the ccd cold reset
             since that already runs through the gsc console and ccd should
	     be unlocked.
         - the gsc will reset the efs boot_mode when it resets the EC.
      - c2d2: gsc_reset
         - gsc_reset resets the GSC. GSC resets boot_mode when its reset
      - 50pin servo: gsc_locked_cold_reset
         - asserts the servo cold reset signal and notifies gsc the EC
	   reset by sending `ecrst pulse`. `ecrst pulse` works when ccd is
	   locked, so boot_mode will work correctly even if ccd is locked. The
	   servo signal will continue to hold the device in reset until
	   cold_reset:off is called.
    There must be an init value for every type of servo. Servo_specific splits
    the device_type at the first '_'. ccd_init applies to all ccd_* devices
    servo_init applies to all servo_* devices. c2d2 applies to c2d2.
  -->
  <control>
    <name>cold_reset_select</name>
    <params servo_init="gsc_locked_cold_reset" c2d2_init="gsc_reset"
    ccd_init="default_cold_reset" init="servo_specific" clobber_ok="patch"/>
  </control>
</root>
